Understood: you want a new method `abs(self) -> Money` on `Money` that returns the absolute amount.

Added `Money::abs` in `src/money.rs` (after `is_negative`):

```rust
/// The same amount without its sign: `-7.10` becomes `7.10`, and a positive amount is unchanged.
pub fn abs(self) -> Money {
    Money(self.0.abs())
}
```

It takes `self` by value, matching `cents()` and `is_negative()`, and reuses `i64::abs` as `Display` already does.

Verified with `cargo test`: compiles clean, all 4 existing tests pass. Note `i64::abs` panics on `i64::MIN`, same as the existing `Display` impl — the amount range the rest of the code works in doesn't reach it.
